            "body": "## Code Review\n\nThis PR removes a hardcoded `log_level: \"info\"` to improve performance. While this change is effective, I've identified a related bug in the handling of `engine_kwargs`. Currently, engine parameters from the configuration are not passed to the SGLang engine, preventing flexible configuration of settings like `log_level`. I've left a comment with details on this issue. Fixing this bug would provide a more robust solution, allowing `log_level` and other SGLang engine parameters to be configured externally without code changes.",
            "comments": {
              "nodes": [
                {
                  "author": {
                    "__typename": "Bot",
                    "login": "gemini-code-assist"
                  },
                  "body": "![high](https://www.gstatic.com/codereviewagent/high-priority.svg)\n\nWhile removing this hardcoded `log_level` improves performance, a more robust solution would be to make it configurable. It appears there's an attempt to support this via `engine_kwargs` (line 421), but these arguments are not correctly passed to the SGLang engine constructor. Currently, only `attention_backend` is used from `engine_kwargs`, and the rest of the configured parameters are silently ignored. This prevents runtime configuration of important engine parameters like `log_level`.\n\nI recommend fixing the `engine_kwargs` handling by merging them into the `args` dictionary before initializing the engine. This would make the system more flexible and avoid the need for hardcoded values or future code changes to tune engine parameters.",
                  "createdAt": "2025-11-12T02:51:56Z",
                  "databaseId": 2516525704,
                  "diffHunk": "@@ -458,7 +458,6 @@ def _init_inference_engine(self, trust_remote_code, actor_module, port):\n                 # NOTE(Chenyang): if you want to debug the SGLang engine output\n                 # please set the following parameters\n                 # Otherwise, it will make the engine run too slow\n-                \"log_level\": \"info\",",
                  "line": null,
                  "originalLine": 461,
